        "original_id": "4f689ef6-9331-5a8c-afbc-c071e9775da0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ronnie Van Zant, Mick Jones, Don Letts, Allen Collins\n- Bands: Lynyrd Skynyrd, The Clash, Big Audio Dynamite\n- Songs and Albums: “That Smell”, Street Survivors\n\nFacts:\n- Ronald Wayne Van Zant was born on January 15, 1948, and he became an American lead vocalist, primary lyricist, and founding member of Lynyrd Skynyrd.\n- Michael Geoffrey “Mick” Jones was born on 26 June 1955 and became a British musician, singer, songwriter, cofounder, lead guitarist, and co-lead vocalist of The Clash.\n- Ronnie Van Zant and Allen Collins wrote the song “That Smell,” which was released in 1977 on the album Street Survivors.\n- Ronnie Van Zant died on October 20, 1977.\n- Mick Jones remained with The Clash until his dismissal in 1983.\n- Don Letts co-founded Big Audio Dynamite with Mick Jones in 1984 and served as the group’s sampler and videographer until departing in 1990.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
